/**
 * Rules Compendium reference index: one entry per rules topic in
 * Wizards of the Coast's D&D 3.5 Rules Compendium, built 2026-11-05
 * from Shaun's PARTIAL copy of the book (uploaded 2026-11-05 as
 * workspace/library-staging/books/rules-compendium-partial.docx).
 *
 * The copy covers only the front of the book: the table of
 * contents, the Introduction, and the alphabetical topics from
 * Ability Score Loss through Energy Drain and Level Loss (printed
 * pp. 5-49 of the book's 160 pages). Topics past the copy
 * (Escape Artist and Use Rope onward) are NOT included, because
 * their text is not in the file. The copy's text came out of a
 * two-column layout, so columns interleave in places; each entry
 * below was reconstructed from what is actually present, and
 * MANIFEST.md in this folder records completeness and garble
 * flags topic by topic.
 *
 * Each summary is a faithful condensation written in our own
 * words — no book prose is reproduced beyond short rule phrases
 * and numbers — carrying the complete operative rule: definitions,
 * DCs, numeric values, stacking and multiplier math, and the
 * exceptions that change outcomes. Designer interludes, essays,
 * and anecdote sidebars printed in the book (Birth of a Rule, The
 * Living Game, and similar) are commentary, not rules, and are
 * skipped; they are listed as skips in the manifest.
 *
 * Entry shape mirrors the house-rules reference index
 * (src/data/homebrew/house-rules-index.ts): reference data for
 * Blendcrafter's Player Reference, not picker collections.
 * `section` is the topic's first letter; the book is alphabetical
 * and the reference filters by section. The Introduction entry is
 * filed under "I" — see the manifest.
 */

