    name: "Cover",
    section: "C",
    ruleset: "core",
    summary:
      "Cover is one of the best defenses available: it protects against attacks (especially ranged attacks) and against being spotted. Standard cover grants a +4 bonus to AC and a +2 bonus on Reflex saves against attacks that originate or burst out from a point on the other side of the cover; spread effects extend around corners and thus negate the cover bonus to Reflex saves. The DM can impose other penalties or restrictions depending on the cover's details — for example, striking effectively through an arrow slit requires a long piercing weapon such as an arrow or spear. Determining cover from a ranged attack: choose a corner of your square; if any line from that corner to any corner of the target's square passes through a square or border that blocks line of effect or provides cover, or through a square occupied by a creature, the target has cover. For a melee attack against an adjacent target, the target has cover if any line from your square to the target's square intersects a wall, including a low wall; melee attacks against a non-adjacent target (such as with a reach weapon) use the ranged-attack rules. Big creatures: a creature with a space larger than 5 feet can choose any square it occupies when determining whether an opponent has cover against its melee attacks, and an attacker can likewise pick any of the squares such a creature occupies when determining whether it has cover. Low obstacles: an obstacle no higher than half your height provides cover, but only to creatures within 30 feet (6 squares) of it; an attacker closer to the obstacle than the target is can ignore this cover. You cannot make attacks of opportunity against an opponent that has cover relative to you. You can use cover to make a Hide check; without cover, you usually need concealment to hide. Forms of cover don't stack — only the best form applies. Improved cover: where cover is especially good (peering around a corner, shooting through an arrow slit), the DM can double the normal bonuses to AC and Reflex saves; the creature effectively gains improved evasion against any attack the Reflex save bonus applies to, and improved cover grants a +10 bonus on Hide checks. Limited cover: an object that doesn't occupy a whole square, such as a tree trunk or pillar, grants a creature standing in the same square a +2 bonus to AC and a +1 bonus on Reflex saves, without otherwise affecting its fighting space. Soft cover: creatures (even enemies) provide cover against ranged attacks, but soft cover grants no bonus on Reflex saves and doesn't allow Hide checks. Total cover: if you don't have line of effect to a target, it has total cover from you and you cannot attack it at all; a spread effect can still reach a creature with total cover if the spread's area covers the distance.",
