    name: "Damage Reduction",
    section: "D",
    ruleset: "core",
    summary:
      "A creature with damage reduction (DR) ignores some of the hit point damage from weapons, natural weapons, and unarmed attacks that don't meet certain criteria — the wound heals immediately or the weapon bounces off harmlessly, and the attacker knows the attack was ineffective. Damage reduction doesn't reduce damage from energy attacks, spells, spell-like abilities, or supernatural abilities, and it doesn't affect poisons or diseases delivered by inhalation, ingestion, or contact. Whenever DR completely negates the damage from an attack, it also negates most special effects accompanying the attack, such as injury poison and injury disease, and an attack that deals no damage because of the target's DR cannot distract the target from concentrating. Stacking: DR from more than one source doesn't stack — the creature gets the benefit of the best DR that applies to a given situation. Reading a DR entry: the amount ignored (usually 5 to 15 points) comes before a slash, followed by the damage type, material, or magic that overcomes it; an attack without the indicated quality has its damage reduced by that amount, to a minimum of 0. Ways to overcome DR: Aligned — chaotic-, evil-, good-, or lawful-aligned weapons overcome entries such as DR 5/lawful; besides inherently aligned magic weapons, alignment can come from an align weapon spell or an alignment subtype, and ammunition fired from an aligned projectile weapon gains that weapon's alignment in addition to any it already has; this DR is supernatural. Damage type — bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing damage overcomes matching entries (a club overcomes DR 5/bludgeoning); this DR is extraordinary. Epic — weapons with a magical enhancement bonus of +6 or higher overcome it (an 'epic weapon' label alone isn't enough), and ammunition from such a weapon counts too; the creature also has the epic strike ability; this DR is supernatural. Magic — a weapon with a +1 or higher enhancement bonus is required, and ammunition from such a weapon counts; the creature also has the magic strike ability; this DR is supernatural. Nothing — an entry with a dash after the slash (DR 5/-) cannot be overcome by any weapon; this insurmountable DR is extraordinary. Special material — adamantine, alchemical silver, or cold iron overcomes matching entries (potent fey, for example, are overcome only by cold iron); DR overcome only by adamantine is extraordinary, while DR overcome only by cold iron or alchemical silver is supernatural. Special situations: 'or' entries (DR 5/cold iron or good) are overcome by a weapon with any one of the listed qualities; 'and' entries (DR 5/silver and good) require a weapon with all of them — and such DR is supernatural if any required quality belongs to a supernatural form of DR, extraordinary otherwise.",
